The abnormal logs contain no new error signature beyond the normal background noise, so I'm settling on one root cause: a network fault on the contacts–preserve connection. Its effect runs through preserve to the dashboard.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-contacts-service",
      "fault_kind": "network_loss",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_source, attr_destination, round(sum(value),1) sum_v FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE metric = 'hubble_drop_total' AND attr_source LIKE '%contacts%' AND attr_destination LIKE '%preserve%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "Hubble drops on contacts→preserve connection total 40 in the abnormal period."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT metric, attr_source, attr_destination, round(sum(value),1) sum_v FROM normal_metrics_sum WHERE metric = 'hubble_drop_total' AND attr_source LIKE '%contacts%' AND attr_destination LIKE '%preserve%' GROUP BY ALL", "claim": "No hubble drop rows exist for contacts→preserve in the normal period."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "WITH c AS (SELECT trace_id, span_id, duration FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND span_name='GET' AND attr_span_kind='Client') SELECT s.service_name, count(*) n, round(avg(c.duration)/1e6,1) client_avg_ms, round(avg(s.duration)/1e6,1) server_avg_ms FROM c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id = c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' WHERE s.service_name='ts-contacts-service' GROUP BY 1", "claim": "Preserve's calls to contacts average about 11 s client-side while contacts' server span averages about 7 ms."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "ts-contacts-service", "to": "ts-preserve-service", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-preserve-service' AND span_name='PreserveController.preserve' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Preserve's PreserveController.preserve p95 is about 54 s in the abnormal period versus about 130 ms-scale normally."}]},
    {"from": "ts-preserve-service", "to": "ts-ui-dashboard", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND span_name='POST /api/v1/preserveservice/preserve' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "The dashboard's preserve requests reach p95 of tens of seconds, so user-facing preserve calls are slow."}]}
  ]
}
```

